{"features_by_type": {"Enabled by default": [{"id": 5169798320357376, "name": "Add javascriptURLs option to SanitizerConfig and Sanitizer", "summary": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12898\n\nSanitizer API also sanitizes javascript:-URLs, when they are used for navigation. This was originally done as a side effect of any \"safe\" method that uses Sanitizer, and omittted for any \"unsafe\" method. The HTML standard recently regularized this and made this a developer-selectable option, instead of a side-effect of a particular method.\n\nBehaviour when the option is not used remains the same.\n", "feature_type_int": 1, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>SecurityFeature>SanitizerAPI"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": ["https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-sanitizer-setjavascripturls"]}, "creator": "vogelheim@google.com", "editors": [], "owners": ["vogelheim@google.com"], "created": {"by": "vogelheim@google.com", "when": "2026-10-08 15:32:06.745055"}, "updated": {"by": "vogelheim@google.com", "when": "2026-10-27 18:44:24.276134"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-10-08 15:32:06.744895", "standards": {"spec": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12898", "maturity": {"text": "Final published standard: Recommendation, Living Standard, Candidate Recommendation, or similar final form", "short_text": "Published standard", "val": 5}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>SecurityFeature>SanitizerAPI"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["vogelheim@google.com"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "Shipped/Shipping", "val": 1}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/86", "notes": "WebKit has not yet implemented the underlying feature (Sanitizer API). I added the position for the larger feature.", "text": "Support", "val": 3}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "No signals", "val": 4, "url": null, "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [5975611616133120], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 6210300985606144, "name": "CORS enforcement for Background Fetch", "summary": "Starting in Chrome 157, the Background Fetch API now enforces Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS). \nThis update aligns Chromium's implementation with the intent of the [Background Fetch spec](https://wicg.github.io/background-fetch/). This ensures that Background Fetch requests are subject to the same security policies as regular Fetch requests, such as Local Network Access checks. \n\nThis update prevents sites from bypassing CORS (and other security policy checks) by using Background Fetch instead of regular [Fetch](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/).", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 2, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": 152, "blink_components": ["Blink>BackgroundFetch"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "cthomp@chromium.org", "editors": ["hchao@chromium.org", "jdeblasio@chromium.org"], "owners": ["cthomp@chromium.org"], "created": {"by": "cthomp@chromium.org", "when": "2026-08-06 17:42:08.457531"}, "updated": {"by": "siobhankeating@google.com", "when": "2026-10-21 10:45:08.808987"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-10-02 16:51:40.107664", "standards": {"spec": "https://wicg.github.io/background-fetch", "maturity": {"text": "Specification being incubated in a Community Group", "short_text": "Incubation", "val": 3}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>BackgroundFetch"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["cthomp@chromium.org"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "No signals", "val": 4, "url": null, "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [6505798957137920], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5152215540039680, "name": "CSS corner shorthand properties ", "summary": "Implements the CSS corner shorthand and per-corner sub-shorthands (corner-top-left, corner-top-right, corner-bottom-left, corner-bottom-right) as well as physical (corner-top, corner-bottom) and logical (corner-block-start, corner-block-end, etc.) edge  shorthands. These allow setting both border-radius and corner-shape for individual corners in a single declaration. Additionally, corners is retained as a compat alias for the corner shorthand.\n\n\nsampler: https://static.januschka.com/i-425897047/\n\nCL: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7747994", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "hjanuschka@gmail.com", "editors": [], "owners": ["hjanuschka@gmail.com"], "created": {"by": "hjanuschka@gmail.com", "when": "2026-04-18 20:53:25.232352"}, "updated": {"by": "hjanuschka@gmail.com", "when": "2026-10-01 18:38:38.786820"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-04-18 20:53:25.232258", "standards": {"spec": "https://drafts.csswg.org/css-borders-4/#corner-shaping", "maturity": {"text": null, "short_text": "Unknown status", "val": 0}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://issues.chromium.org/issues/425897047", "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["hjanuschka@gmail.com"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/823", "notes": "General standards-position discussion for CSS corner shaping. The                                                                                                                                                                                            \n   corner shorthands are an ergonomic extension that combines the existing                                                                                                                                                                                      \n   corner-shape and border-radius properties.", "text": "Positive", "val": 3}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/229", "notes": "WebKit supports the underlying CSS corner-shaping proposal. These                                                                                                                                                                                            \n   shorthands combine corner-shape and border-radius without adding new                                                                                                                                                                                         \n   rendering capabilities. \n\nsee: https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/74191 ", "text": "In development", "val": 2}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "No signals", "val": 4, "url": null, "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [5125404290580480], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5136856479039488, "name": "CSS position-visibility:anchor{s}-valid", "summary": "The `anchors-valid` value was implemented as part of https://crbug.com/329703412 but subsequently reverted, due to spec questions about the exact definition of the value. Since that time, the value has been renamed to `anchor-valid` (see https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136123851571200) and also better defined to be clear that only the default anchor matters, resolving a lot of ambiguity, and making this value shippable.", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "masonfreed@google.com", "editors": ["masonfreed@google.com"], "owners": ["masonf@chromium.org"], "created": {"by": "masonfreed@google.com", "when": "2026-09-23 22:23:43.562609"}, "updated": {"by": "masonfreed@google.com", "when": "2026-09-29 22:14:03.563777"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-09-23 22:23:43.562480", "standards": {"spec": "https://drafts.csswg.org/css-anchor-position-1/#position-visibility", "maturity": {"text": "Final published standard: Recommendation, Living Standard, Candidate Recommendation, or similar final form", "short_text": "Published standard", "val": 5}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://crbug.com/333421963", "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["masonf@chromium.org"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1457", "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "Shipped/Shipping", "val": 1}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "No signals", "val": 4, "url": null, "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [6066954614996992], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5178263526834176, "name": "CSS text-decoration-inset", "summary": "CSS text-decoration-inset controls how far underlines, overlines, and line-through decorations are inset from or extended beyond text run edges. It supports auto, length, and percentage values, including one-value and two-value syntax for setting the start and end offsets. This lets developers adjust decoration spacing and create reveal effects with native text decorations instead of background gradients or additional elements.\n\n\nsampler: https://static.januschka.com/i-468928416/?asddsaasd\nMDN: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/text-decoration-inset\n\nCL: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7748204", "feature_type_int": 1, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "hjanuschka@gmail.com", "editors": ["chrishtr@chromium.org", "jakearchibald@chromium.org"], "owners": ["hjanuschka@gmail.com"], "created": {"by": "hjanuschka@gmail.com", "when": "2026-04-10 11:30:04.696752"}, "updated": {"by": "hjanuschka@gmail.com", "when": "2026-10-15 23:03:53.703981"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-08-17 19:39:43.204396", "standards": {"spec": "https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-decor-4/#propdef-text-decoration-inset", "maturity": {"text": null, "short_text": "Unknown status", "val": 0}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://issues.chromium.org/issues/468928416", "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["hjanuschka@gmail.com"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": "Firefox shipped `text-decoration-inset` in Firefox 146. Support for percentage values is still in progress: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Firefox/Releases/146#css", "text": "Shipped/Shipping", "val": 1}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": "WebKit has implemented `text-decoration-inset`, but support for percentage values is still pending. Implementation: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319178. Percentage support: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322441", "text": "Shipped/Shipping", "val": 1}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "No signals", "val": 4, "url": null, "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [5125366508290048], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 6294595288825856, "name": "CSS text-overflow: <string> value", "summary": "Adds a <string> value to the text-overflow property.\n\nThis allows web authors to specify a custom string (e.g., \"(more)\") to indicate that text has been clipped. This provides more design flexibility and can be used to create more user-friendly and context-aware overflow indicators.", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "jja08111@gmail.com", "editors": [], "owners": ["jja08111@gmail.com"], "created": {"by": "jja08111@gmail.com", "when": "2026-08-18 05:34:17.605213"}, "updated": {"by": "jja08111@gmail.com", "when": "2026-10-19 08:04:45.453117"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-10-19 08:04:45.453117", "standards": {"spec": "https://drafts.csswg.org/css-overflow-4/#text-overflow", "maturity": {"text": "Specification currently under development in a Working Group", "short_text": "Working draft", "val": 4}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://issues.chromium.org/issues/41492459", "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["jja08111@gmail.com"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": "https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=312156", "notes": "Some of the new WPTs are broken because of two cases.\n- Clipping the rendering of the ellipsis itself if there is insufficient space for the ellipsis.\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/css-overflow-4/#ellipsing-details\n- Suppressing line breaks as Ruby.\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12557", "text": "Shipped/Shipping", "val": 1}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/72631", "notes": "The PR has been merged but it's not released yet.", "text": "Shipped/Shipping", "val": 1}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "No signals", "val": 4, "url": null, "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [6362078184079360], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5107682460696576, "name": "Capability Elements Icon-only mode", "summary": "Introduces a new attribute to render Capability Elements(<camera>, <microphone> and <geolocation>) as compact icon buttons without text using a `displaymode` attribute. This gives developers flexible UI density for spatial layouts such as map controls and video floating trays while preserving native security guarantees and full screen reader accessibility.\n\nThis is an extension to the recently released Capability Elements\nhttps://chromestatus.com/feature/5153829504024576", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["UI>Browser>Permissions>Prompts"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "ravjit@google.com", "editors": [], "owners": ["ravjit@google.com", "tungnh@google.com"], "created": {"by": "ravjit@google.com", "when": "2026-09-22 11:27:08.620287"}, "updated": {"by": "ravjit@google.com", "when": "2026-10-16 12:51:25.579278"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-09-22 11:27:08.620175", "standards": {"spec": "https://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-extensions/#media-capture-html-elements", "maturity": {"text": "Final published standard: Recommendation, Living Standard, Candidate Recommendation, or similar final form", "short_text": "Published standard", "val": 5}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": null, "blink_components": ["UI>Browser>Permissions>Prompts"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["ravjit@google.com", "tungnh@google.com"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "No signals", "val": 4, "url": null, "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [6578539041259520], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5069584943153152, "name": "Expose ProgressEvent in service workers", "summary": "ProgressEvent is available in service workers, allowing developers to construct progress events with lengthComputable, loaded, and total attributes.\nThis aligns service workers with other worker contexts and the XMLHttpRequest Standard.", "feature_type_int": 1, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "choiwonik91@gmail.com", "editors": [], "owners": ["choiwonik91@gmail.com"], "created": {"by": "choiwonik91@gmail.com", "when": "2026-09-24 12:40:58.450084"}, "updated": {"by": "choiwonik91@gmail.com", "when": "2026-10-07 15:23:58.298801"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-09-24 12:40:58.449959", "standards": {"spec": "https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-progressevent", "maturity": {"text": "Final published standard: Recommendation, Living Standard, Candidate Recommendation, or similar final form", "short_text": "Published standard", "val": 5}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://issues.chromium.org/issues/332663431", "blink_components": ["Blink"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["choiwonik91@gmail.com"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": "https://hg.mozilla.org/releases/mozilla-release/raw-file/FIREFOX_140_0_RELEASE/dom/webidl/ProgressEvent.webidl", "notes": "Verified in Firefox 140 release sources: ProgressEvent is exposed to\nWindow and Worker, and ServiceWorkerGlobalScope includes the Worker global name. This establishes service worker exposure in a released version; it does not identify the first supported version.\n\nServiceWorker global definition:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/releases/mozilla-release/raw-file/FIREFOX_140_0_RELEASE/dom/webidl/ServiceWorkerGlobalScope.webidl", "text": "Shipped/Shipping", "val": 1}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/WebKit/blob/WebKit-7614.1.25.0.30/Source/WebCore/dom/ProgressEvent.idl", "notes": "Verified in Apple's published WebKit-7614.1.25.0.30 source distribution:\nProgressEvent is exposed to Window and Worker, and ServiceWorkerGlobalScope includes the Worker global name. This is release-source evidence, not a claim about the first supported Safari version.\n\nServiceWorker global definition:\nhttps://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/WebKit/blob/WebKit-7614.1.25.0.30/Source/WebCore/workers/service/ServiceWorkerGlobalScope.idl", "text": "Shipped/Shipping", "val": 1}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "No signals", "val": 4, "url": null, "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [5455043309469696], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5172548013916160, "name": "HTML-in-canvas", "summary": "HTML-in-canvas enables customizing the rendering of html using canvas with new primitives to manage canvas layout, drawing capabilities, rendering events for DOM-to-canvas synchronization, and geometry update capabilities for canvas-to-DOM synchronization.", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>Canvas"], "resources": {"samples": ["https://github.com/WICG/html-in-canvas#demos"], "docs": []}, "creator": "aaronhk@chromium.org", "editors": ["vmpstr@chromium.org"], "owners": ["chrishtr@chromium.org", "schenney@chromium.org", "pdr@chromium.org", "szager@chromium.org", "foolip@chromium.org"], "created": {"by": "aaronhk@chromium.org", "when": "2024-06-26 18:07:01.756076"}, "updated": {"by": "pdr@chromium.org", "when": "2026-10-27 09:26:30.644634"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-09-29 23:58:11.875353", "standards": {"spec": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11588", "maturity": {"text": "Specification currently under development in a Working Group", "short_text": "Working draft", "val": 4}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://crbug.com/500967896", "blink_components": ["Blink>Canvas"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["chrishtr@chromium.org", "schenney@chromium.org", "pdr@chromium.org", "szager@chromium.org", "foolip@chromium.org"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "In development", "val": 3}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1076", "notes": "", "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/630", "notes": "WebKit has begun early implementation work in https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/70542.", "text": "Positive", "val": 3}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "Positive", "val": 2, "url": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10650#issuecomment-3324124682", "notes": "We have positive signals from users of the Dev Trial and Origin Trials: https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10650#issuecomment-3324124682"}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [5086580804157440], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5087964794322944, "name": "Language Detector API on Android", "summary": "Exposes the LanguageDetector JavaScript Web API on Chrome for Android (Clank). This allows web applications to detect text languages locally on mobile devices using fast, privacy-preserving, and offline-capable on-device machine learning models and not rely on cloud endpoints.", "feature_type_int": 1, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": 153, "blink_components": ["Blink > AI > Translator %26 Language Detector"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "jaeone@google.com", "editors": ["msw@google.com", "reillyg@google.com", "dbogadi@google.com", "dbogadi@chromium.org"], "owners": ["jaeone@google.com"], "created": {"by": "jaeone@google.com", "when": "2026-08-20 21:32:06.861619"}, "updated": {"by": "jaeone@google.com", "when": "2026-10-16 19:14:49.056037"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-09-24 16:43:41.092354", "standards": {"spec": "https://webmachinelearning.github.io/translation-api", "maturity": {"text": "Specification being incubated in a Community Group", "short_text": "Incubation", "val": 3}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://crbug.com/549896512", "blink_components": ["Blink > AI > Translator %26 Language Detector"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["jaeone@google.com"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1015", "notes": null, "text": "Negative", "val": 7}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/339", "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "Positive", "val": 2, "url": null, "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [5445570348056576], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5171478175809536, "name": "Long Animation Frames style and layout duration", "summary": "Add `styleDuration` and `forcedStyleDuration` information to the Long Animation Frame API, enabling developers to distinguish style and layout times.", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>PerformanceAPIs"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "yoavweiss@chromium.org", "editors": [], "owners": ["yoavweiss@chromium.org"], "created": {"by": "yoavweiss@chromium.org", "when": "2026-01-19 10:10:59.090990"}, "updated": {"by": "yoavweiss@chromium.org", "when": "2026-10-16 00:48:58.680211"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-09-30 13:06:33.430750", "standards": {"spec": "https://github.com/w3c/long-animation-frames/pull/30", "maturity": {"text": "Specification being incubated in a Community Group", "short_text": "Incubation", "val": 3}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://issues.chromium.org/issues/476826067", "blink_components": ["Blink>PerformanceAPIs"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["yoavweiss@chromium.org"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": "Positive on the broader LoAF: https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/929\n\nI'm asking if I should file a more specific issue for these extra attributes.", "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/283", "notes": "No signal for the broader LoAF feature. Unlikely they'd have a strong position on these attributes.", "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "Positive", "val": 2, "url": "https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/qvGqBcSOFTQ/m/5DCTOu9KCgAJ", "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [5156342375514112], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5054329641893888, "name": "Renewed HTML insertion&streaming methods", "summary": "Expose multiple HTML setting methods that provide a coherent story for dynamically inserting markup into an existing document.\n\n- Positional methods (before/after/append/prepend/replaceWith) that take HTML as argument, effectively replacing insertAdjacentHTML.\n- Streaming methods (stream{Append}HTML{Unsafe}) which return a WritableStream, receiving text as input and parsing HMHL.\n- Passing {runScripts} as part of SetHTMLUnsafeOptions, mimicking createContextualFragment behavior.\n- Supporting createParserOptions in trusted types, allowing trusted types to override scripting mode and sanitizer.", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>HTML>Parser"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "nrosenthal@chromium.org", "editors": [], "owners": ["nrosenthal@chromium.org", "foolip@chromium.org"], "created": {"by": "nrosenthal@chromium.org", "when": "2026-03-11 13:53:37.879524"}, "updated": {"by": "nrosenthal@chromium.org", "when": "2026-10-19 09:02:56.839626"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-10-19 09:02:56.839626", "standards": {"spec": "https://github.com/WICG/declarative-partial-updates/blob/main/dynamic-markup-revamped-explainer.md#resulting-api", "maturity": {"text": "Specification currently under development in a Working Group", "short_text": "Working draft", "val": 4}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://issues.chromium.org/issues/491743369", "blink_components": ["Blink>HTML>Parser"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com", "barrypollard@google.com"], "owners": ["nrosenthal@chromium.org", "foolip@chromium.org"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1370", "notes": "(It's in \"suggests positive\" state)", "text": "Positive", "val": 3}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/629", "notes": "Note: WebKit folks have been active in the feature's design, despite not filing an official positive position yet.", "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "Positive", "val": 2, "url": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2142", "notes": "See also https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10122"}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [4564172388040704], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5136123851571200, "name": "Ship anchor-visible and anchor-valid, and deprecate the plural versions", "summary": "The CSSWG resolved to rename `anchors-valid` --> `anchor-valid` [1] and `anchors-visible` --> `anchor-visible` [2]. To accomplish this, we'll rename the properties to the singular variants, and add aliases from the plural versions to the singular versions. At a later date, we will remove the plural variants. This chromestatus is only about shipping the new versions, and deprecating the old ones (but not removing them).\n\n[1] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10201#issuecomment-4180411971\n[2] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10201#issuecomment-4390233490", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "masonfreed@google.com", "editors": ["masonfreed@google.com"], "owners": ["masonf@chromium.org"], "created": {"by": "masonfreed@google.com", "when": "2026-09-23 20:38:00.469167"}, "updated": {"by": "masonfreed@google.com", "when": "2026-10-05 13:15:45.580507"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-09-23 20:38:00.469042", "standards": {"spec": "https://drafts.csswg.org/css-anchor-position-1/#position-visibility", "maturity": {"text": "Final published standard: Recommendation, Living Standard, Candidate Recommendation, or similar final form", "short_text": "Published standard", "val": 5}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://issues.chromium.org/issues/526682332", "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["masonf@chromium.org"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "Shipped/Shipping", "val": 1}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "No signals", "val": 4, "url": null, "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [6482554105495552], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5138797158334464, "name": "Web Bluetooth: Make BluetoothRemoteGATTServer an EventTarget", "summary": "BluetoothRemoteGATTServer inherits from EventTarget, exposing the standard addEventListener(), removeEventListener(), and dispatchEvent() methods. This enables connection-level events to be dispatched directly on the GATT server.\n", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>Bluetooth"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "hjanuschka@gmail.com", "editors": [], "owners": ["hjanuschka@gmail.com"], "created": {"by": "hjanuschka@gmail.com", "when": "2026-09-05 14:48:29.274428"}, "updated": {"by": "hjanuschka@gmail.com", "when": "2026-10-07 15:03:01.524333"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-09-05 14:48:29.274239", "standards": {"spec": "https://pr-preview.s3.amazonaws.com/hjanuschka/web-bluetooth/pull/672.html#bluetoothremotegattserver", "maturity": {"text": "Specification currently under development in a Working Group", "short_text": "Working draft", "val": 4}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40265040", "blink_components": ["Blink>Bluetooth"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["hjanuschka@gmail.com"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/95", "notes": "Firefox does not implement Web Bluetooth. The citation is Mozilla's position on the overall Web Bluetooth API, not a separate position on this inheritance change.\n", "text": "Negative", "val": 7}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/570", "notes": "Safari does not implement Web Bluetooth. The citation is WebKit's position on the overall Web Bluetooth API, not a separate position on this inheritance change.\n", "text": "Oppose", "val": 7}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "Positive", "val": 2, "url": null, "notes": "this is a small preparation feature for the larger demanded: https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40265040"}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": "The WebBluetoothCG specification change is approved in https://github.com/WebBluetoothCG/web-bluetooth/pull/672 but has not yet merged.\n"}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [6501983497355264], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 4882016087703552, "name": "WebGPU: atomic-vec2u-min-max", "summary": "Allows the use of 64-bit atomic minimum and maximum operations on `atomic<vec2u>` in WGSL.\n\nThis provides WebGPU shader authors with a way to implement certain algorithms that use 64-bit atomics without requiring full support for 64-bit integers.", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>WebGPU"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "jrprice@google.com", "editors": ["cwallez@google.com", "dneto@google.com", "fbeaufort@google.com"], "owners": ["jrprice@google.com", "dsinclair@google.com"], "created": {"by": "jrprice@google.com", "when": "2026-09-21 21:17:17.144228"}, "updated": {"by": "jrprice@google.com", "when": "2026-09-29 17:21:13.459157"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-09-21 21:17:17.144013", "standards": {"spec": "https://www.w3.org/TR/webgpu/#dom-gpufeaturename-atomic-vec2u-min-max", "maturity": {"text": "Final published standard: Recommendation, Living Standard, Candidate Recommendation, or similar final form", "short_text": "Published standard", "val": 5}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://crbug.com/453689550", "blink_components": ["Blink>WebGPU"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["jrprice@google.com", "dsinclair@google.com"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/pull/5610", "notes": "Feedback indicated via WebGPU standardization process.", "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/pull/5610", "notes": "Specification approval constitutes a positive signal, per https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/294#issuecomment-1877411933", "text": "Positive", "val": 3}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "Positive", "val": 2, "url": "https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/issues/5071#issuecomment-2660636760", "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [4555101229416448], "finch_urls": []}], "Deprecated": [], "Removed": [], "Stepped rollout": [{"id": 5068439115923456, "name": "Disconnect WebSockets on BFCache entry", "summary": "Chrome is changing its behavior to allow pages with active WebSocket connections to enter the Back/Forward Cache. To achieve this, active WebSockets are now disconnected when a page is cached. Previously, active WebSocket connections prevented pages from entering BFCache.\n\nTo revert to the previous behavior (preventing pages with active WebSockets from entering BFCache), we previously provided a [BackForwardCacheForWebSocketsAllowed](https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#BackForwardCacheForWebSocketsAllowed) policy. Admins can set this policy to _Disabled_ , which will prevent breakage in legacy apps that lack WebSocket reconnection logic. This policy will be deprecated in Chrome 157. \n\nFor more information on BFCache, see [Test back/forward cache](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/devtools/application/back-forward-cache).", "feature_type_int": 2, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 2, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": 148, "blink_components": ["Blink>Network>WebSockets"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "annasato@google.com", "editors": ["fergal@google.com"], "owners": ["annasato@google.com", "fergal@google.com", "gilbertoc@google.com", "denomoto@google.com"], "created": {"by": "annasato@google.com", "when": "2026-04-13 03:58:42.624927"}, "updated": {"by": "siobhankeating@google.com", "when": "2026-10-21 10:48:07.561316"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-10-13 01:16:29.697465", "standards": {"spec": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12349", "maturity": {"text": "Final published standard: Recommendation, Living Standard, Candidate Recommendation, or similar final form", "short_text": "Published standard", "val": 5}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://g-issues.chromium.org/issues/467838624", "blink_components": ["Blink>Network>WebSockets"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["annasato@google.com", "fergal@google.com", "gilbertoc@google.com", "denomoto@google.com"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1390", "notes": null, "text": "Positive", "val": 3}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/648", "notes": null, "text": "Shipped/Shipping", "val": 1}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "Positive", "val": 2, "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7376981348709756928?commentUrn=urn%3Ali%3Acomment%3A%28activity%3A7376981348709756928%2C7377217740341747712%29&replyUrn=urn%3Ali%3Acomment%3A%28activity%3A7376981348709756928%2C7377954189664129024%29&dashCommentUrn=urn%3Ali%3Afsd_comment%3A%287377217740341747712%2Curn%3Ali%3Aactivity%3A7376981348709756928%29&dashReplyUrn=urn%3Ali%3Afsd_comment%3A%287377954189664129024%2Curn%3Ali%3Aactivity%3A7376981348709756928%29", "notes": "In this post, Wix explains how BFCache helped raise their global Core Web Vitals pass rate from 61% to 75%. They identified WebSocket connections from chat widgets as a key blocker. This reflects a common challenge where developers lack control over WebSockets in third-party scripts, and feedback on this effort has been very positive."}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null}], "Origin trial": [{"id": 5657801797009408, "name": "Connection Allowlists - Embedded Enforcement", "summary": " Connection Allowlists (https://chromestatus.com/feature/5175745573945344) is a feature designed to provide explicit control over external endpoints by restricting connections initiated via the Fetch API or other web platform APIs from a document or worker. This aspect of the feature extends Connection Allowlists to support embedded enforcement on iFrames and nested documents/workers. This allows the parent document to enforce restrictions on embedded content where they can choose to opt in or not load.\n\nMore details on the proposal can be found here: https://github.com/WICG/connection-allowlists ", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 2, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": 150, "blink_components": ["Blink>SecurityFeature>ConnectionAllowlist"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "brandonm@chromium.org", "editors": ["averge@chromium.org", "mkwest@chromium.org"], "owners": ["brandonm@chromium.org", "brandm@microsoft.com"], "created": {"by": "brandonm@chromium.org", "when": "2026-06-16 18:12:16.736114"}, "updated": {"by": "brandm@microsoft.com", "when": "2026-10-08 21:03:26.692117"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-06-16 18:12:16.736005", "standards": {"spec": "https://wicg.github.io/connection-allowlists/#issue-d96e905e", "maturity": {"text": "Specification being incubated in a Community Group", "short_text": "Incubation", "val": 3}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>SecurityFeature>ConnectionAllowlist"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["brandonm@chromium.org", "brandm@microsoft.com"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1322", "notes": null, "text": "Positive", "val": 3}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/583", "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "Positive", "val": 2, "url": "https://github.com/WICG/connection-allowlists/issues/1", "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [6175678484578304], "origin_trial_id": "3609072151384031233", "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5261280285949952, "name": "Overscroll Areas", "summary": "This feature adds a set of primitives to allow elements to anchor to overscroll areas of other elements. It further allows these elements to be revealed with swipe gestures, similar to scrollers.", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>Scroll"], "resources": {"samples": ["https://flackr.github.io/web-demos/html/overscrollcontainer"], "docs": []}, "creator": "vmpstr@chromium.org", "editors": [], "owners": ["vmpstr@chromium.org", "flackr@chromium.org"], "created": {"by": "vmpstr@chromium.org", "when": "2025-09-08 14:38:21.611642"}, "updated": {"by": "flackr@chromium.org", "when": "2026-10-14 08:02:52.140712"}, "accurate_as_of": "2025-09-08 14:38:21.611399", "standards": {"spec": "https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/14532", "maturity": {"text": "Specification currently under development in a Working Group", "short_text": "Working draft", "val": 4}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://issues.chromium.org/443719046", "blink_components": ["Blink>Scroll"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["vmpstr@chromium.org", "flackr@chromium.org"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "Positive", "val": 2, "url": null, "notes": "We had some developer trial feedback to indicate interest."}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [5642678951870464], "finch_urls": []}], "In developer trial (Behind a flag)": [{"id": 5069051687731200, "name": "CSS flow-start and flow-end alignment keywords", "summary": "Introduce the flow-start/end keywords as value aliases for the existing flex-start/end keywords as resolved in the CSSWG. These are needed for alignment in the case of placement reversals.\n\nflow-start in CSS Grid-Lanes would indicate the starting edge of the container at which placement begins, which is useful in the case where placement is reversed (`fill-reverse`, `track-reverse`, discussed in this CSSWG issue: [css-grid-3][masonry] item-flow row vs. column in masonry layouts \u00b7 Issue #12803 \u00b7 w3c/csswg-drafts).  Because these are acting as value aliases, we expect flex-start/end to follow the logical directions in Grid Lanes, as well, which will expand the definition of these keywords from only applying special behavior in flexbox to applying to any layout mode whose logical start/end is different from its physical start/end.\n\nFor serialization, if either flex-start/end  or flow-start/end  is used, the returned serialized value should be flow-start/end.", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "celestepan@microsoft.com", "editors": [], "owners": ["celestepan@microsoft.com", "almaher@microsoft.com", "yanlingwang@microsoft.com", "mhochk@microsoft.com"], "created": {"by": "celestepan@microsoft.com", "when": "2026-08-27 23:11:08.503217"}, "updated": {"by": "celestepan@microsoft.com", "when": "2026-10-21 18:32:33.417295"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-10-19 17:46:10.654306", "standards": {"spec": "https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/14539", "maturity": {"text": null, "short_text": "Unknown status", "val": 0}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://issues.chromium.org/issues/555299635", "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["celestepan@microsoft.com", "almaher@microsoft.com", "yanlingwang@microsoft.com", "mhochk@microsoft.com"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1455#issuecomment-5839398061", "notes": null, "text": "Positive", "val": 3}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/723", "notes": null, "text": "N/A", "val": 9}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "No signals", "val": 4, "url": null, "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [4812286597398528], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5136856479039488, "name": "CSS position-visibility:anchor{s}-valid", "summary": "The `anchors-valid` value was implemented as part of https://crbug.com/329703412 but subsequently reverted, due to spec questions about the exact definition of the value. Since that time, the value has been renamed to `anchor-valid` (see https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136123851571200) and also better defined to be clear that only the default anchor matters, resolving a lot of ambiguity, and making this value shippable.", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "masonfreed@google.com", "editors": ["masonfreed@google.com"], "owners": ["masonf@chromium.org"], "created": {"by": "masonfreed@google.com", "when": "2026-09-23 22:23:43.562609"}, "updated": {"by": "masonfreed@google.com", "when": "2026-09-29 22:14:03.563777"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-09-23 22:23:43.562480", "standards": {"spec": "https://drafts.csswg.org/css-anchor-position-1/#position-visibility", "maturity": {"text": "Final published standard: Recommendation, Living Standard, Candidate Recommendation, or similar final form", "short_text": "Published standard", "val": 5}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://crbug.com/333421963", "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["masonf@chromium.org"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": "https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1457", "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "Shipped/Shipping", "val": 1}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "No signals", "val": 4, "url": null, "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [5222529684865024], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5155080092385280, "name": "Decisions API", "summary": "Provides high-speed, deterministic semantic decision-making directly on the user's device as a built-in AI capability.\n\nUnlike open-ended generative language models (such as the Prompt API) that decode text token-by-token over hundreds or thousands of milliseconds, the Decisions API (window.DecisionModel) evaluates natural language input text against a structured set of questions and candidate options in a single forward pass using logit scoring. This delivers micro-latency evaluations (tens or low hundreds of milliseconds on typical consumer laptop CPUs and GPUs) while outputting calibrated confidence values.\n\nThis brings non-autoregressive \"System 1\" decision models (e.g. Jev, Laya, Kev, Open-Jev) natively into the web platform, providing developers with a pragmatic, zero-marginal-cost \"Semantic If\" primitive for real-time client-side routing, interactive input guardrails, and adaptive user interfaces.", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 2, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": 156, "blink_components": ["Blink>AI"], "resources": {"samples": ["https://web-ai.studio/playgrounds/decisions"], "docs": []}, "creator": "msw@chromium.org", "editors": ["etiennenoel@google.com", "dbogadi@google.com", "msw@google.com"], "owners": ["msw@chromium.org", "kenjibaheux@chromium.org"], "created": {"by": "msw@chromium.org", "when": "2026-10-01 05:48:51.560065"}, "updated": {"by": "msw@google.com", "when": "2026-10-14 18:58:44.163410"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-10-01 05:48:51.559925", "standards": {"spec": null, "maturity": {"text": "Proposal in a personal repository, no adoption from community", "short_text": "Pre-incubation", "val": 2}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://issues.chromium.org/issues/568193538", "blink_components": ["Blink>AI"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["msw@chromium.org", "kenjibaheux@chromium.org"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "No signals", "val": 4, "url": null, "notes": "Excitement from the community as seen from folks building with Jev, Laya, and Open-Jev. We want to help validate the potential and have been encouraged by inbound requests from partners looking for lightweight, sub-50ms triage sieves ahead of deeper LLM calls or other steps. Some of those partners have confirmed sufficient value even with the heavier Prompt API option, and would welcome a more efficient capability, leaving full LLM inferencing for subsequent steps (e.g. improving internal moderation processes)."}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": "We intend to collaborate with the community within the W3C WebML CG, exploring shared alignment on decision models alongside our existing joint Built-in AI efforts."}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [6049213766041600], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5091965583622144, "name": "Popup Capability Delegation", "summary": "Allows Service Workers to delegate their transient popup capability (acquired from a user interaction like a notification click) to same-origin client windows. This enables client windows to open child (pop-up) windows, such as email previews or chat windows, without being blocked by the popup blocker. This allows developers to take advantage of frame state-sharing performance (e.g. sharing in-memory state via `window.opener`), instead of requiring a new top-level browsing context (which is what `Clients.openWindow` does).", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["UI>Notifications"], "resources": {"samples": ["https://googlechrome.github.io/samples/service-worker/capability-delegation-popup/index.html"], "docs": ["https://github.com/WICG/capability-delegation/blob/main/explainers/popup-delegation.md"]}, "creator": "dmurph@google.com", "editors": [], "owners": ["dmurph@google.com"], "created": {"by": "dmurph@google.com", "when": "2026-08-03 20:41:21.466027"}, "updated": {"by": "dmurph@google.com", "when": "2026-10-13 03:29:16.102977"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-08-03 20:41:21.465912", "standards": {"spec": null, "maturity": {"text": null, "short_text": "Unknown status", "val": 0}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://issues.chromium.org/issues/542314185", "blink_components": ["UI>Notifications"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["dmurph@google.com"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "Positive", "val": 2, "url": "https://github.com/WICG/capability-delegation/issues/42", "notes": "Directly requested by web application partners (e.g., email and chat applications) that need certain notification clicks to open lightweight auxiliary/preview popup windows sharing state with an existing client window rather than forcing a full top-level navigation via clients.openWindow()."}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [4893195436687360], "finch_urls": []}, {"id": 5136123851571200, "name": "Ship anchor-visible and anchor-valid, and deprecate the plural versions", "summary": "The CSSWG resolved to rename `anchors-valid` --> `anchor-valid` [1] and `anchors-visible` --> `anchor-visible` [2]. To accomplish this, we'll rename the properties to the singular variants, and add aliases from the plural versions to the singular versions. At a later date, we will remove the plural variants. This chromestatus is only about shipping the new versions, and deprecating the old ones (but not removing them).\n\n[1] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10201#issuecomment-4180411971\n[2] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10201#issuecomment-4390233490", "feature_type_int": 0, "unlisted": false, "enterprise_impact": 1, "enterprise_product_category": 0, "breaking_change": false, "confidential": false, "first_enterprise_notification_milestone": null, "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "resources": {"samples": [], "docs": []}, "creator": "masonfreed@google.com", "editors": ["masonfreed@google.com"], "owners": ["masonf@chromium.org"], "created": {"by": "masonfreed@google.com", "when": "2026-09-23 20:38:00.469167"}, "updated": {"by": "masonfreed@google.com", "when": "2026-10-05 13:15:45.580507"}, "accurate_as_of": "2026-09-23 20:38:00.469042", "standards": {"spec": "https://drafts.csswg.org/css-anchor-position-1/#position-visibility", "maturity": {"text": "Final published standard: Recommendation, Living Standard, Candidate Recommendation, or similar final form", "short_text": "Published standard", "val": 5}}, "browsers": {"chrome": {"bug": "https://issues.chromium.org/issues/526682332", "blink_components": ["Blink>CSS"], "devrel": ["devrel-chromestatus-all@google.com"], "owners": ["masonf@chromium.org"], "origintrial": false, "prefixed": null, "flag": false, "status": {"text": "Proposed", "val": 2}, "announced": false}, "ff": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "No signal", "val": 5}}, "safari": {"view": {"url": null, "notes": null, "text": "Shipped/Shipping", "val": 1}}, "webdev": {"view": {"text": "No signals", "val": 4, "url": null, "notes": null}}, "other": {"view": {"notes": null}}}, "is_released": false, "milestone": null, "roadmap_stage_ids": [4793704245231616], "finch_urls": []}]}, "total_count": 23}